WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.744
Du Fu was a great poet of the Tang dynasty; he was in his forties when the An Lushan Rebellion broke out.

00:00:07.094 --> 00:00:12.518
He walked mountain roads and villages, stepping personally into a world in turmoil.

00:00:12.868 --> 00:00:17.956
He saw with his own eyes the suffering the war brought, with the common people displaced and homeless.

00:00:18.306 --> 00:00:22.554
Many families left their homes and supported one another on the road.

00:00:22.904 --> 00:00:29.432
In that chaotic age, Du Fu picked up his brush and wrote poem after poem.

00:00:29.782 --> 00:00:34.342
He carefully wrote everything he saw into his poems.

00:00:34.692 --> 00:00:41.124
His poems recorded the war and the people's lives, and later generations called them 'poetry-history'.

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:44.906
Reading his poems is like seeing the face of that era itself.

00:00:45.256 --> 00:00:50.512
Because of these immortal works, people honored him as the 'Poet-Sage'.

00:00:50.862 --> 00:00:54.774
Later readers of his poems all deeply admired him.

00:00:55.124 --> 00:01:01.244
More than a thousand years have passed, and Du Fu's poems still move countless readers.

